From 265c0ab68fb50bedd0102536eb92612a3eb1af91 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sven Panne <sven.panne@checkmk.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 17:40:01 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] 22918 SEC Fix stack buffer overflow in mkevent

mkevent -n built its message in an 8 KB stack buffer without checking
its length and read out of bounds for negative numbers, and plain
messages could end up unterminated. Use a std::string, cut off after
8191 bytes, but not within a character.

Backport: Patch set 4 of this change fixes the old code of 2.5.0 and
2.4.0. They lack the commits before this one and the single write() of
message and newline, which conflicts trivially.

Jira-Ref: CMK-40742
Change-Id: Id29f5c5181cdd2241a11939dbaa44cc98bf2e6e4
